  "body": "**Description:**\r\nI'm sure there's a good reason for allowing public access to the profile API calls but if one tries to keep them private, problems arise.\r\n\r\n- Say I know that a user that nicks `dudebro` in other internet presences.\r\n- Say I know the HS of `dudebro` or that I simply want to probe whether this is the case\r\n\r\n1. I'd then check `/_matrix/client/r0/profile/%40dudebro%3Ahomeserver.bro`\r\n2. If I get a hit, there's no way of stopping me from using the value of `avatar_url` to gain access to `dudebro`'s avatar image by enter it into the well-known public media path of the synapse server: `https://homeserver.bro/_matrix/media/v1/thumbnail/homeserver.bro/AVATAR_URL?width=800&height=800\r\n\r\nIn the context of private HS instances, user expectancy is definitely that sensitive data such as avatars or even just displaynames are kept private. Since I assume this publicness has to do with federation I suggest an option to limit this exploit.",
